('d72f61a7-4f90-52c6-8246-fef936482a2c', '8695e833-9d29-4367-bfd6-0c20aebb2b1d', '2df83c3e-834f-517a-a55c-cf1ff80eccfb', 'a-level', '31.3', '9702 coursebook 31.3 · Stellar radii: Wien and Stefan–Boltzmann', 9, 9, 'Betelgeuse emits most strongly at a wavelength of 830 nm. Calculate its surface temperature. Take the Wien constant = 2.90 × 10⁻³ m K.', NULL, 1, 'numeric'::answer_type, '3494', 'K', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'T = 2.90 × 10⁻³ ÷ 830 × 10⁻⁹ = 3490 K. Mark scheme (2 marks). C1: λmax T = constant. A1: T = 3490 K.', 2, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 420 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg56faaf0b-t fg56faaf0b-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg56faaf0b-t">Spectrum of Betelgeuse</title><desc id="fg56faaf0b-d">Black-body spectrum of Betelgeuse: relative intensity against wavelength from 0 to 2500 nm, peaking at 830 nm, with the visible band 400–700 nm shaded.</desc><line x1="24" y1="34" x2="24" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="99.6" y1="34" x2="99.6" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="175.2" y1="34" x2="175.2" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="250.8" y1="34" x2="250.8" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="326.4" y1="34" x2="326.4" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="402" y1="34" x2="402" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="242" x2="402" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-