('60c295a5-698f-57b2-80cf-6feaaadceb7d', '8695e833-9d29-4367-bfd6-0c20aebb2b1d', '2df83c3e-834f-517a-a55c-cf1ff80eccfb', 'a-level', '31.3', '9702 coursebook 31.3 · Stellar radii: Wien and Stefan–Boltzmann', 43, 43, 'Sirius A has a luminosity of 9.7 × 10²⁷ W and its spectrum peaks at 290 nm. (a) Calculate its surface temperature. (b) Calculate its radius. Give only the answer to (b), in units of 10⁹ m. Take the Wien constant = 2.90 × 10⁻³ m K and σ = 5.67 × 10⁻⁸ W m⁻² K⁻⁴.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.167', '10⁹ m', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) T = 2.90 × 10⁻³ ÷ 290 × 10⁻⁹ = 1.00 × 10⁴ K. (b) r = √(9.7 × 10²⁷ ÷ (4π × 5.67 × 10⁻⁸ × (1.00 × 10⁴)⁴)) = 1.17 × 10⁹ m. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: T. M1: r = √(L/4πσT⁴). C1: substitution. C1: value. A1: r = 1.17 × 10⁹ m.', 5, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 420 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgdd0ff773-t fgdd0ff773-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgdd0ff773-t">Spectrum of Sirius A</title><desc id="fgdd0ff773-d">Black-body spectrum of Sirius A: relative intensity against wavelength from 0 to 1500 nm, peaking at 290 nm, with the visible band shaded.</desc><line x1="24" y1="34" x2="24" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="99.6" y1="34" x2="99.6" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="175.2" y1="34" x2="175.2" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="250.8" y1="34" x2="250.8" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="326.4" y1="34" x2="326.4" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:roun