d"/><text x="241" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">150</text><line x1="311.5" y1="242" x2="311.5" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="311.5" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">200</text><line x1="382" y1="242" x2="382" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="382" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">250</text><line x1="25.4" y1="242" x2="29.4" y2="242" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="22.4" y="242" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0</text><line x1="25.4" y1="190" x2="29.4" y2="190" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="22.4" y="190" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">5</text><line x1="25.4" y1="138" x2="29.4" y2="138" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="22.4" y="138" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">10</text><line x1="25.4" y1="86" x2="29.4" y2="86" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="22.4" y="86" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">15</text><line x1="25.4" y1="34" x2="29.4" y2="34" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="22.4" y="34" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">20</text><text x="205.7" y="274" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">distance d / Mpc</text><text x="25.4" y="14" font-size="14" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">recession speed v / 10³ km s⁻¹</text><polyline points="29.4,242 382,60" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:6 4"/><polyline points="29.4,96.4 311.5,96.4" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:3 3"/><polyline points="311.5,242 311.5,96.4" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:3 3"/><line x1="307.5" y1="92.4" x2="315.5" y2="100.4" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="307.5" y1="100.4" x2="315.5" y2="92.4" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/></svg>', 'A galaxy plotted at distance 200 Mpc and recession speed 1.4 × 10⁴ km s⁻¹, on a line through the origin.'),
('70dd8ae6-6949-568b-a2b6-e024afce8c6b', '8695e833-9d29-4367-bfd6-0c20aebb2b1d', '397b2565-7a2c-5e16-a138-021d30b81dd9', 'a-level', '31.4', '9702 coursebook 31.4 · Hubble’s law and the Big Bang', 30, 30, 'A galaxy recedes at 4.5 × 10⁶ m s⁻¹. The hydrogen line at 656 nm is redshifted. Calculate the observed wavelength in nm. Take c = 3.00 × 10⁸ m s⁻¹.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '665.8 nm', 'nm', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'λ = 656 × (1 + 4.5 × 10⁶ ÷ 3.00 × 10⁸) = 665.8 nm. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: Δλ = λv/c. C1: add to λ. A1: λ = 665.8 nm.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('e207cd31-355a-5fa0-b684-88202cf74f7e', '8695e833-9d29-4367-bfd6-0c20aebb2b1d', '397b2565-7a2c-5e16-a138-021d30b81dd9', 'a-level', '31.4', '9702 coursebook 31.4 · Hubble’s law and the Big Bang', 31, 31, 'Which observation is the strongest evidence for the Big Bang, besides galaxy redshifts?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'The cosmic microwave background radiation, uniform in all directions', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'It is the cooled radiation from the early Universe. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: CMB. C1: uniform, black-body. A1: A (The cosmic microwave background radiation, uniform in all directions).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('5fa51e35-4319-5dbe-9090-9e4ade20a113', '8695e833-9d29-4367-bfd6-0c20aebb2b1d', '397b2565-7a2c-5e16-a138-021d30b81dd9', 'a-level', '31.4', '9702 coursebook 31.4 · Hubble’s law and the Big Bang', 32, 32, 'Galaxy A is 3.0 times as far away as galaxy B. Calculate (recession speed of A) ÷ (recession speed of B).', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '3', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'v ∝ d: ratio = 3.0 ÷ 1 = 3.0. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: Hubble''s law. C1: value. A1: ratio = 3.0.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('c073b6ae-80f9-552e-be08-666ad5e3c286', '8695e833-9d29-4367-bfd6-0c20aebb2b1d', '397b2565-7a2c-5e16-a138-021d30b81dd9', 'a-level', '31.4', '9702 coursebook 31.4 · Hubble’s law and the Big Bang', 33, 33, 'A quasar''s light shows Δλ/λ = 0.15. Assuming v = cΔλ/λ and H₀ = 2.3 × 10⁻¹⁸ s⁻¹, calculate its distance in units of 10²⁵ m. Take c = 3.00 × 10⁸ m s⁻¹.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.957', '10²⁵ m', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'v = 0.15 × 3.00 × 10⁸ = 4.5 × 10⁷ m s⁻¹. d = 4.5 × 10⁷ ÷ 2.3 × 10⁻¹⁸ = 1.96 × 10²⁵ m. Mark scheme (4 marks). C1: v. C1: d = v/H₀. C1: value. A1: d = 1.96 × 10²⁵ m.', 4, NULL, NULL),
('8e15aceb-c5f0-595c-b2b4-99ec080eb204', '8695e833-9d29-4367-bfd6-0c20aebb2b1d', '397b2565-7a2c-5e16-a138-021d30b81dd9', 'a-level', '31.4', '9702 coursebook 31.4 · Hubble’s law and the Big Bang', 34, 34, 'The redshift of distant galaxies is not caused by them all moving away from a central point. What is the modern interpretation?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'Space itself is expanding, stretching the light as it travels', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Every observer sees the same pattern. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: expansion of space. C1: no centre. A1: D (Space itself is expanding, stretching the light as it travels).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('9d340d7a-3734-56c5-8a3e-6065112ac445', '8695e833-9d29-4367-bfd6-0c20aebb2b1d', '397b2565-7a2c-5e16-a138-021d30b81dd9', 'a-level', '31.4', '9702 coursebook 31.4 · Hubble’s law and the Big Bang', 35, 35, 'A galaxy has a recession speed of 2.0 × 10⁷ m s⁻¹ and a distance of 9.0 × 10²⁴ m. Calculate H₀ from these values, in units of 10⁻¹⁸ s⁻¹.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '2.222', '10⁻¹⁸ s⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'H₀ = v/d = 2.0 × 10⁷ ÷ 9.0 × 10²⁴ = 2.22 × 10⁻¹⁸ s⁻¹. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: H₀ = v/d. C1: value. A1: H₀ = 2.22 × 10⁻¹⁸ s⁻¹.', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg1e8d2e07-t fg1e8d2e07-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg1e8d2e07-t">Galaxy on a Hubble graph</title><desc id="fg1e8d2e07-d">A galaxy plotted at distance 9.0 × 10²⁴ m and recession speed 2.0 × 10⁷ m s⁻¹, on a line through the origin.</desc><line x1="33" y1="34" x2="33" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="102.8" y1="34" x2="102.8" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="172.6" y1="34" x2="172.6" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="242.4" y1="34" x2="242.4" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="312.2" y1="34" x2="312.2" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="382" y1="34" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="33" y1="242" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d