 text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">wavelength / nm</text></svg>', 'A line at 486.1 nm in the laboratory spectrum appears at 518.0 nm in the spectrum of a galaxy.'),
('51e72445-f222-58ee-9826-088ca3a33513', '8695e833-9d29-4367-bfd6-0c20aebb2b1d', '397b2565-7a2c-5e16-a138-021d30b81dd9', 'a-level', '31.4', '9702 coursebook 31.4 · Hubble’s law and the Big Bang', 50, 50, 'The cosmic microwave background peaks at a wavelength of 1.06 mm. (a) Calculate its temperature. (b) Explain why this supports the Big Bang. Take the Wien constant = 2.90 × 10⁻³ m K.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '2.736', 'K', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) T = 2.90 × 10⁻³ ÷ 1.06 × 10⁻³ = 2.74 K. (b) It is the expected black-body glow of the hot early Universe, stretched to microwaves by expansion. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: mm to m. M1: Wien. C1: value. B1: cooled remnant of hot early Universe. A1: T = 2.74 K.', 5, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 420 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg8aa0d8e1-t fg8aa0d8e1-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg8aa0d8e1-t">Cosmic microwave background</title><desc id="fg8aa0d8e1-d">Black-body spectrum of the cosmic microwave background: relative intensity against wavelength from 0 to 5 mm, peaking at 1.06 mm.</desc><line x1="24" y1="34" x2="24" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="99.6" y1="34" x2="99.6" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="175.2" y1="34" x2="175.2" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="250.8" y1="34" x2="250.8" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="326.4" y1="34" x2="326.4" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="402" y1="34" x2="402"