('bf202c61-9ab2-5999-b026-fa44fdead445', '8695e833-9d29-4367-bfd6-0c20aebb2b1d', '397b2565-7a2c-5e16-a138-021d30b81dd9', 'a-level', '31.4', '9702 coursebook 31.4 · Hubble’s law and the Big Bang', 51, 51, 'Galaxy X shows Δλ/λ = 0.020 and galaxy Y shows Δλ/λ = 0.050. (a) Calculate both recession speeds. (b) Taking H₀ = 2.3 × 10⁻¹⁸ s⁻¹, calculate the distance between them if they lie in the same direction from us, in units of 10²⁴ m. Take c = 3.00 × 10⁸ m s⁻¹.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '3.913', '10²⁴ m', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) X: 0.020 × 3.00 × 10⁸ = 6.0 × 10⁶ m s⁻¹; Y: 0.050 × 3.00 × 10⁸ = 1.5 × 10⁷ m s⁻¹. (b) Δd = (1.5 × 10⁷ − 6.0 × 10⁶) ÷ 2.3 × 10⁻¹⁸ = 3.91 × 10²⁴ m. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: speed X. C1: speed Y. M1: d = v/H₀ for each. C1: difference. C1: value. A1: Δd = 3.91 × 10²⁴ m.', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 460 190" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg00faf34f-t fg00faf34f-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg00faf34f-t">Two galaxies in one direction</title><desc id="fg00faf34f-d">Galaxies X (Δλ/λ = 0.020) and Y (Δλ/λ = 0.050) lie in the same direction from the Earth; the distance between them is to be found.</desc><line x1="46" y1="62" x2="414" y2="62" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:5 4"/><circle cx="46" cy="62" r="6" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="46" y="32" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">Earth</text><path d="M177.2,62 A16,7 0 1,0 209.2,62 A16,7 0 1,0 177.2,62" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="193.2" cy="62" r=